    "c1": {
      "anchor": "i1",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Spanish: a default on an inherited built-in member compiles under its Spanish name",
      "excerpt": "Spanish: a default on an inherited built-in member compiles under its Spanish name",
      "text": "Unclear whether this is fixed for good or not",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-09T14:44:05.093Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T14:45:28.133Z",
          "html": "<p>The bug this issue reports is fixed for good. One related spelling still doesn't work, and it's a separate limit that English has too.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>\n    <b>Fixed, with tests that keep it fixed:</b> a line giving an inherited member a value now compiles by the member's own name.\n    <ul>\n      <li><code>su candado es \"bloqueado\"</code> compiles to <code>get lock() { return \"locked\" }</code>.</li>\n      <li><code>su dirección es abajo</code> compiles to <code>get direction() { return \"down\" }</code>.</li>\n      <li><code>&lt;encanto-página \"inicio\" bloqueado&gt;</code> compiles to the same lock.</li>\n      <li>Run again today on the latest <code>main</code>: all 52 tests in that file pass.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n  <li>\n    <b>Still an error, in both languages:</b> the lock's value without quotes.\n    <ul>\n      <li><code>su candado es bloqueado</code> says: No entiendo \"bloqueado\".</li>\n      <li><code>its lock is locked</code> says: Don't understand \"locked\".</li>\n      <li>It stops with a clear error. It doesn't compile to the wrong thing.</li>\n      <li>The lock's words aren't known as bare values on a line like this, the way <code>abajo</code> is for direction.</li>\n    </ul>\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<epic-net-effect>\n  <ul>\n    <li>The Spanish name bug is gone: nothing more to do for it, so this issue can be approved and closed.</li>\n    <li>If you want <code>its lock is locked</code> to work without quotes, leave a note here and it becomes its own todo.</li>\n  </ul>\n</epic-net-effect>"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "at": "2026-11-09T15:17:49.297Z",
          "text": "send to language epic as a new phase",
          "edited": "2026-11-09T15:17:58.730Z"
        },
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-09T15:18:21.663Z",
          "html": "<p>Sent to epic <code>language</code> as request r14, to become a new phase there: a lock's value without quotes doesn't parse, in either language.</p>\n<epic-net-effect>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Nothing about the unquoted form is left in this epic.</li>\n    <li>This issue's own bug is fixed, so it can be approved and closed.</li>\n  </ul>\n</epic-net-effect>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
